  "note": "A single pale mast leans toward the south bank over the Han. Unequal fans of stays run in the median above the six-lane deck. A flared tower pier and repeating concrete approach piers support the crossing, which curves into the interchanges at either end. The viewer uses a fixed sea-level datum. The modeled south approach rises above the ridge in the standard elevation data. The mapped bearing lines set the ends and the separate ramp links retain their native geometry."
